\p{Filed under [[conf-neuromod-nyc-2026]], category 3 (writing energy into the brain — here optical, not electrical). No people in the photo.}

\image{conf-photobiomodulation-children.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} \strong{Transcranial photobiomodulation (tPBM)} — near-infrared light to the head — as an adjunct within a comprehensive rehabilitation program for children (n=129) with neurodevelopmental disorders, including autism. Preliminary results: the tPBM group showed larger improvements than controls across behavioral symptoms (impulsivity, aggression, social interaction) with high tolerance and no adverse events reported. A non-electrical modality on the "write-in" axis — optical dosing rather than a field.}
